WEBVTT

0
00:00.170 --> 00:01.310
<v Krista>In this video we're going to be talking</v>

1
00:01.310 --> 00:04.150
about multiplication and division of simple fractions.

2
00:04.150 --> 00:06.280
And, really, when we talk about multiplication

3
00:06.280 --> 00:07.660
and division of fractions,

4
00:07.660 --> 00:10.340
we're just talking about multiplication of fractions,

5
00:10.340 --> 00:11.910
and I'll show you why in a second.

6
00:11.910 --> 00:14.090
So, we're going to start with this first example here.

7
00:14.090 --> 00:16.000
It's a multiplication problem with fractions.

8
00:16.000 --> 00:17.690
We have the fraction one half

9
00:17.690 --> 00:20.060
times the fraction three over 10.

10
00:20.060 --> 00:22.370
And when we're multiplying fractions it's actually,

11
00:22.370 --> 00:24.540
in a way, a lot easier than even adding

12
00:24.540 --> 00:27.070
and subtracting fractions because all we do

13
00:27.070 --> 00:29.210
is multiply our numerators together

14
00:29.210 --> 00:30.840
to get our new numerator,

15
00:30.840 --> 00:33.320
and we multiply our denominators together

16
00:33.320 --> 00:35.130
to get our new denominator.

17
00:35.130 --> 00:37.810
So we say, one times three is three,

18
00:37.810 --> 00:39.100
we get our new numerator.

19
00:39.100 --> 00:42.790
And two times 10 is 20, we get our new denominator.

20
00:42.790 --> 00:44.650
And that's it, all we have to do is make sure

21
00:44.650 --> 00:46.810
that our fraction is simplified as much as possible,

22
00:46.810 --> 00:48.610
meaning that it's in lowest terms,

23
00:48.610 --> 00:49.960
our answer's in lowest terms,

24
00:49.960 --> 00:51.820
and as long as it is, then we're done.

25
00:51.820 --> 00:54.530
And, in fact, three and 20 have no common factors,

26
00:54.530 --> 00:57.410
so this is simplified or reduced as much as possible.

27
00:57.410 --> 00:59.980
And, so, three over 20 is our final answer.

28
00:59.980 --> 01:01.460
If we look at another example here,

29
01:01.460 --> 01:03.760
we have three over five, or three fifths,

30
01:03.760 --> 01:05.740
times six over four.

31
01:05.740 --> 01:07.560
And if we multiply these together,

32
01:07.560 --> 01:12.370
we get three times six is 18, so our new numerator is 18.

33
01:12.370 --> 01:15.800
Our denominator we get five times four is 20,

34
01:15.800 --> 01:17.010
our new denominator,

35
01:17.010 --> 01:18.950
and now, we just need to reduce this.

36
01:18.950 --> 01:21.830
Both the numerator and denominator are even numbers

37
01:21.830 --> 01:24.550
so we know we can divide both of them by two.

38
01:24.550 --> 01:29.550
18 divided by two is nine, 20 divided by two is 10,

39
01:29.970 --> 01:31.980
so we've reduced the fraction,

40
01:31.980 --> 01:34.620
we can't reduce nine tenths any further,

41
01:34.620 --> 01:36.650
so this is going to be our final answer.

42
01:36.650 --> 01:39.760
So, multiplication of fractions is just as simple as that,

43
01:39.760 --> 01:41.460
multiply the numerators together,

44
01:41.460 --> 01:43.150
multiply the denominators together,

45
01:43.150 --> 01:45.210
and reduce the answer if you can.

46
01:45.210 --> 01:48.470
Division of fractions is only slightly more complicated.

47
01:48.470 --> 01:50.000
All we're going to do is turn this

48
01:50.000 --> 01:52.470
into a multiplication problem, and here's how we do it.

49
01:52.470 --> 01:54.550
When we have one fraction divided by another,

50
01:54.550 --> 01:58.280
so in this example we have one half divided by one third.

51
01:58.280 --> 01:59.940
All we're going to do is take the fraction

52
01:59.940 --> 02:02.110
that's being divided, the second fraction,

53
02:02.110 --> 02:03.930
and we're going to find it's reciprocal,

54
02:03.930 --> 02:05.670
meaning we're going to flip it upside down.

55
02:05.670 --> 02:07.180
So, we're going to change the places

56
02:07.180 --> 02:08.680
of the numerator and denominator.

57
02:08.680 --> 02:12.560
So, the reciprocal of one over three is three over one,

58
02:12.560 --> 02:14.810
we just put the denominator and the numerator,

59
02:14.810 --> 02:16.630
and the numerator and the denominator,

60
02:16.630 --> 02:18.540
so we flip their places.

61
02:18.540 --> 02:19.960
And when we flip the places,

62
02:19.960 --> 02:22.610
when we find the reciprocal of this fraction,

63
02:22.610 --> 02:25.270
then instead of doing division, we do multiplication.

64
02:25.270 --> 02:26.810
So, we're going to leave this first fraction

65
02:26.810 --> 02:28.630
exactly as it is, one half.

66
02:28.630 --> 02:31.390
Instead of division, we're going to do multiplication,

67
02:31.390 --> 02:34.120
and then we're just going to flip this fraction upside down.

68
02:34.120 --> 02:37.580
So, instead of one over three, we'll get three over one,

69
02:37.580 --> 02:39.880
and now this is just a multiplication problem,

70
02:39.880 --> 02:41.370
it's as simple as that.

71
02:41.370 --> 02:43.600
So, again, just like with multiplication,

72
02:43.600 --> 02:46.210
one times three, in the numerators, is three.

73
02:46.210 --> 02:48.760
Two times one, in the denominators, is two,

74
02:48.760 --> 02:51.790
and we have our final answer of three over two.

75
02:51.790 --> 02:52.990
We'll do a second example here.

76
02:52.990 --> 02:56.110
We have five eights, divided by two thirds.

77
02:56.110 --> 02:59.520
Again, we'll leave the first fraction as is, five eights.

78
02:59.520 --> 03:02.110
Instead of doing division, we'll do multiplication.

79
03:02.110 --> 03:03.620
And then we'll take our second fraction

80
03:03.620 --> 03:04.620
and flip it upside down.

81
03:04.620 --> 03:08.030
So, instead of two over three, we'll do three over two.

82
03:08.030 --> 03:09.770
And then this is a multiplication problem

83
03:09.770 --> 03:11.850
and we just multiply straight across.

84
03:11.850 --> 03:15.900
So, five times three, in the numerators, gives us 15.

85
03:15.900 --> 03:19.000
Eight times two, in the denominators, gives us 16,

86
03:19.000 --> 03:21.830
and our final answer is 15 over 16.

87
03:21.830 --> 03:24.050
So that's how you do division with fractions.

88
03:24.050 --> 03:25.700
One thing to note, you might see

89
03:25.700 --> 03:27.770
fraction division problems written this way.

90
03:27.770 --> 03:30.450
Instead of five eights divided by two thirds

91
03:30.450 --> 03:32.130
with our division sign like this,

92
03:32.130 --> 03:34.600
you might see it like this, five eights

93
03:34.600 --> 03:36.710
divided by two thirds.

94
03:36.710 --> 03:39.130
In other words, one large fraction,

95
03:39.130 --> 03:41.720
with fractions in the numerator and the denominator.

96
03:41.720 --> 03:43.210
It's just the same thing.

97
03:43.210 --> 03:45.660
These two things, right here, mean the same thing.

98
03:45.660 --> 03:48.410
This is five eights divided by two thirds.

99
03:48.410 --> 03:51.070
So, when you see this, you can take the numerator,

100
03:51.070 --> 03:55.200
five eights, and just say, instead of divided by two thirds,

101
03:55.200 --> 03:57.810
you can multiply by whatever you get

102
03:57.810 --> 03:59.670
when you flip this denominator upside down.

103
03:59.670 --> 04:02.760
So, instead of two over three, you do three over two,

104
04:02.760 --> 04:05.060
and now you have a fraction multiplication problem,

105
04:05.060 --> 04:06.120
just like we did here.

106
04:06.120 --> 04:09.220
And you multiply across and you get 15 over 16.

107
04:09.220 --> 04:11.450
So, that's how you do multiplication and division

108
04:11.450 --> 04:12.773
with simple fractions.